From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] contacts: buttons to edit and to call a contact
Description:
 Each entry of the contacts page gets a button that opens the contact in
 the contact view of the dialer and a button that calls the contact right
 away; a tap on the entry still puts the number into the dial pad. For a
 contact with several numbers the number is asked for first. The buttons
 are flat, their icons are drawn in the text colour, and they are two and a
 half grid units wide and high (RowIconButton), a touch target as Kirigami
 asks for.
 .
 Builds on the contact view (patch 0001 of this series).
Forwarded: no
License: as the patched files (LGPL-2.0-or-later, LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL); new file components/RowIconButton.qml LGPL-2.0-or-later
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
